.TH CLOODOO 1 "2026" "cloodoo" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cloodoo \- personal TODO system with a retro TUI and multi-device sync
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cloodoo
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cloodoo
is a personal TODO system featuring a retro terminal user interface,
real-time multi-device sync over gRPC with mutual TLS, LLM-powered
enrichment of tasks, and companion Android, GNOME Shell, and browser
extension apps.
.PP
Run without a command,
.B cloodoo
starts the interactive TUI. Press
.B ?
inside the TUI for the key bindings.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add \fITITLE\fR
Add a new TODO. Options:
.B \-p
priority (high, medium, low),
.B \-s
scheduled date and
.B \-d
due date (YYYY\-MM\-DD, \fItoday\fR, \fItomorrow\fR, or a day name),
.B \-t
tag (repeatable),
.B \-n
note,
.B \-a
attach a file (screenshot, document, etc.).
.TP
.B list
List TODOs.
.B \-a
includes completed items;
.B \-p
and
.B \-s
filter by priority and status.
.TP
.B done \fIID\fR
Mark a TODO as completed.
.TP
.B stats
Show TODO statistics.
.TP
.B export
Export TODOs in org-agenda format.
.B \-\-pdf
produces PDF (requires pandoc, wkhtmltopdf, or enscript),
.B \-o
sets the output path,
.B \-t
groups by tag instead of date,
.B \-a
includes completed items.
.TP
.B lists
Manage user-defined lists (grocery, movies, etc.).
.TP
.B context
Manage the user context supplied to the LLM for enrichment.
.TP
.B dump
Dump the SQLite database as SQL statements.
.TP
.B compact
Remove superseded historical versions from the temporal database to
reclaim space.
.TP
.B sync-server
Start the gRPC streaming sync server.
.B \-b
bind address,
.B \-p
gRPC port (default 50051),
.B \-\-hostname
public hostname for ACME HTTPS and pairing URLs,
.B \-\-no\-tls
disables TLS for testing.
.TP
.B sync-connect
Start the TUI connected to a remote sync server
.RB ( \-h
host,
.B \-p
port,
.B \-\-client\-cert
and
.B \-\-client\-key
for mTLS).
.TP
.B sync-upload-attachments
Upload all local attachments to the sync server.
.TP
.B sync-reset
Force a full resync by resetting the last-sync timestamp.
.TP
.B cert
Manage mTLS certificates:
.B cert issue \fINAME\fR
creates a client certificate and shows a QR code for pairing the
Android app.
.TP
.B user
Manage users for multi-user sync.
.TP
.B invite
Manage invite codes for self-service registration.
.TP
.B setup-extension
(alias:
.B install-native-host
)
Register the browser extension's native messaging host for Chrome,
Chromium, and Firefox in the current user's profile. Not needed when
cloodoo was installed from the RPM or DEB package, which register the
host system-wide.
.TP
.B native-host
Native messaging host for the browser extension (started by the
browser; internal use).
.TP
.B enrich-pending
Enrich TODOs that are pending enrichment (internal use).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cloodoo/cloodoo.db
Main SQLite database (temporal, append-only, WAL mode).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/cloodoo/certs/
Certificate authority and client certificates for sync.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cloodoo/config.lisp
LLM provider configuration: \fB:provider\fR (:gemini, :openai,
:anthropic, :ollama), \fB:model\fR, \fB:api\-key\-env\fR, and optional
\fB:endpoint\fR for OpenAI-compatible or Ollama servers.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cloodoo/user-context.md
Personal context supplied to the LLM for better tag and priority
inference.
.TP
.I ~/.config/cloodoo/sync-config.lisp
Server hostname and port for automatic sync connection.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The LLM API key is read from the environment variable named by
.B :api\-key\-env
in the configuration file (for example
.BR GEMINI_API_KEY ,
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY ,
or
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Add a task due tomorrow:
.B cloodoo add \(dqRenew passport\(dq \-p high \-d tomorrow \-t errands
.TP
Start a sync server:
.B cloodoo sync-server \-\-hostname todo.example.com
.TP
Pair a device:
.B cloodoo cert issue phone
.TP
Export this week's agenda to PDF:
.B cloodoo export \-\-pdf \-o agenda.pdf
